Z||000000||PAUL88GT||01-05-2000||12:27 PM||||I saw the words "Limited Edition" a GT below the quarter window. What extras did this version come with? It looked like a regular GT to me. TIA.||||reg||5
Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-05-2000||02:22 PM||||My guess paul is that it was a regular GT.  Often dealers put graphics on cars and charge more for a "Limited Edition" version of the car.  In other words that $.30 decal set could have made them $1000.  Otherwise it could have been owner installed.  For instance you can even get quarter windows (for notchbacks) from Paul McKibben that say anything that you want.  Yes, some even say "Limited Edition".  This is of course just speculation.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000003||Formula||01-05-2000||02:23 PM||||I saw a Limited edition quarter panel for sale on the web somewhere.<P>If it was gold then it was a Autozone rebadge that you can buy for a couple bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||01-05-2000||07:57 PM||||That was on Paul's site.  His quarter windows are great and rather affordable for us notchbackers... here is the address <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails</A> <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000005||Voyd||01-05-2000||11:32 PM||||hmm, i have a question which is kinda related. on my 85SE i have an "SS" incription near the fender on both sides. this is not a decal, its protruding. its loooks pretty good, but i doubt its stock...||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||01-06-2000||09:52 AM||||I have an 85 4cyl that had a small metal badge on the map pocket that read: <P>Fiero 500LE<BR>Limited Edition<BR>One of One Hundred.<P>I searched and searched and searched and could find no mention of any LE series of 100 cars, so I am relatively sure that this was a badge made in a mall somewhere.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||01-06-2000||07:15 PM||||DJ,<P>That sounds like another dealer installed "options package".  Usually they are nice graphics etc.  If yours is text only then chances are that some past owner had it made up. <P>Voyd,<P>I used to work at a body side molding company.  People had Impala SS, Jimmy, S-10, Sunfire and the like raised PVC insignias everywhere.  The favorite location was on the 30 yard dumpster.  Chances are yours was something that came from an autoparts store somewhere.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||01-07-2000||12:58 PM||||Probably was...the car also has some 500LE lettering on the doors, which I thought was tacky looking, but at least that little badge was tastefully done.||||reg||1
Z||000009||PAUL88GT||01-07-2000||01:42 PM||||This "Limited Edition" decal or trim piece was located down near or on the lower ground effect trim under the quarter window.  It looked factory, but I would not doubt that a dealer would put someting on there to get a better sales price. I was just curious if this came on several of the GTs, but is sounds as though it did not.  I may try to ask the owner if I am in that area again. ||||reg||1
