Z||000012||william_thorniii||01-07-2000||08:37 PM||||Monkey,<P>Need I mention that for $1500 it isn't even cowl induction... just looks like it.  I didn't want to use your wifes car as an example but it the perfect one.  A couple of stickers and a fake cowl induction all taped to the car and mark it up outrageously.. It would be really cool though if you could make that cowl work!<P>Formula,<P>I totally agree with you about the Impala.  I have always been drawn to station wagons.  My dream modern (well almost) is a 90's Caprice wagon, Impala trim, black, lowered, tubbed and a supercharged big-block.. not to mention the monstrous blower blocking any possible view out the front.  Car and Driver did a story on a John Moss 454 bhp Impala Wagon... the title read "Mrs. Vader, your wagon is ready!"<P>William T. Thorn, III<P>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Monkeyman||01-08-2000||07:12 AM||||William--Feel free to use my wifes car as an example anytime.  You know how I feel about it.  It's an overpriced piece of plastic crap.  And, yes it would be cool if the hood scoop worked.  It could be done, but since it's just glued on it would take alot of work.  For those of you who don't know my wifes car, it's a '98 Cav 4 cyl, auto, fancy hubcaps, A/C, and that's it other than the stickers, hood scoop and rear spoiler.  No other options.  It is kind of a nice purple.||||reg||1
Z||000014||william_thorniii||01-09-2000||02:37 AM||||Monkey, <P>The first step is to find another purple Cav hood in a bone yard.  Next step... get out the Sawz-all.  The next thing that you know you are driving around a Cav with working cowl induction... of course you would need to slightly modify the airbox. <P>William T. THorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000015||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||05:33 AM||||Yes, but then I'd have to modify the anemic 2.2L 4 banger.  (Maybe a 502ci BB under the hood?!)  Then I'd feel the need to put something other than 70 series tires under it.  Etc, etc.  I'd rather spend the money on my Fiero. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It would be cool to do, but there would be alot of fiberglass work involved and I don't have the time for that.  Besides, I don't know where I'd buy another scoop like that if I broke it.  It's sold by a company in Springboro called Trim Accessories.  They are even more worthless than the Cav.  We've had numerous problems with the spoiler and they won't do anything about it.||||reg||1
